course: dictionary
lesson: 361
title: Antibacterial: killing germs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Antibacterial is a long word, but you can break it into two parts. Anti means against, and bacteria are tiny living things, some of which cause illness. So antibacterial means against bacteria: it kills them or stops them from growing. «Ordinary soap works well, and antibacterial soap has not been shown to be better for everyday use.» The sentence tells you that antibacterial soap is a kind of soap, and that it does not automatically work better than ordinary soap.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. The sentence says ordinary soap "works well", so antibacterial soap is being compared with it. It is not presented as magic. Ask yourself: what would fit in this place? Then swap in your meaning, "killing bacteria", and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Antibacterial does not mean "kills everything". Bacteria are only one kind of germ. Colds and flu are caused by viruses, and antibacterial things do not kill viruses. So an antibacterial hand gel does not cure a cold.
fact: Antibacterial means killing bacteria or stopping them from growing.
fact: Bacteria are tiny living things, and some of them can make us ill.
fact: Antibacterial soap, antibacterial wipes and antibacterial spray are all examples of products that work against bacteria.
fact: Antibacterial things do not kill viruses, such as the viruses that cause colds and flu.
fact: Rarely, an antibacterial is a substance that does this job, such as a cleaning spray.
exercise: «Ordinary soap works well, and antibacterial soap has not been shown to be better for everyday use.» What does antibacterial mean here? | Able to cure a cold | Made of plastic | *Killing bacteria or stopping them from growing | Smelling of flowers
exercise: Antibacterial wipes are used to clean the kitchen table. What do antibacterial wipes do? | They are made of paper | *They kill bacteria or stop them growing | They make the table shiny | They cure a cold
exercise: Mia says her antibacterial hand gel will cure her cold. Why is she wrong? | *Antibacterial things kill bacteria, not viruses like the ones that cause colds | Colds are never caused by any germs | Hand gel can only be used on the feet | Gel is only for washing hair
test: What does antibacterial mean? | Killing all animals | *Killing bacteria or stopping them from growing | Making things dirty | Making things hot
test: Which of these is an antibacterial product? | Plain tap water | A woolly jumper | Ordinary bread | *Antibacterial spray
exam: Which sentence about antibacterial is correct? | Antibacterial things kill viruses that cause colds and flu | *Antibacterial things kill or stop bacteria, but not viruses | Antibacterial soap is always better than ordinary soap | Antibacterial means very old
